{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nThe diagonal morphism for relative schemes is an immersion.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta_{X/S}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-diagonal-immersion}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b8b07a9e29081aee33ac0a75e7656bad20442ebc8d1a3c817fae3cd7918196a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c6d2b81bd9de78727cd1f65f9a213b4cb0cda7b749bc04f438112360edc9077f", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme over <MATH_0002>.\nThe diagonal morphism <MATH_0003> is an immersion.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:93749ad80fe177e5b9a4909aea03266a04de73b215aeb2798317ac1f75113c73", "unit_id": "tag:01KJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V \\subset X$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\subset S$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\times_U V$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0005": "$W$", "MATH_0006": "$X \\times_S X$", "MATH_0007": "$V \\times_U V$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Delta_{X/S}^{-1}(V \\times_U V) \\to V \\times_U V$", "MATH_0009": "$V = \\Delta_{X/S}^{-1}(V \\times_U V)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\Delta_{V/U}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fibre-product-affines}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-open-fibre-product}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-closed-local-target}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-diagonal-affines-closed}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d29a122ee8dbede1302eef66c94516c31ab9ca3443be873ef0a3fa856b37c70c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:179e49b5d80d644c1afaad1a2b18f0325573e369c02ab8f270147c0af31093cb", "source_text": "Recall that if <MATH_0001> is affine open and maps into\n<MATH_0002> affine open, then <MATH_0003> is affine open\nin <MATH_0004>, see Lemmas <REF_0001>\nand <REF_0002>.\nConsider the open subscheme <MATH_0005> of <MATH_0006> which\nis the union of these affine opens <MATH_0007>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0003> it is enough\nto show that each morphism\n<MATH_0008> is\na closed immersion. Since <MATH_0009>\nwe are just checking that <MATH_0010> is a closed\nimmersion, which is Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:97da3f2487577bf78d454e14e741952a57947dd9450cd5ed3d6f744f6027d9c8", "unit_id": "tag:01KJ:proof"}
